From: Luiz Angelo Daros de Luca <luizluca@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] net: dsa: realtek: backport rtl8365mb bridge, FDB and VLAN offload

Backport the net-next realtek_forward series through commit 660a9e399ab0 onto Linux 6.18.33.
This brings rtl8365mb bridge join/leave, FDB, VLAN and bridge port flag offload support.

Includes the accepted tag_rtl8_4 REASON-code handling present in net-next.

Signed-off-by: Luiz Angelo Daros de Luca <luizluca@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Sven Rademakers <sven@turingpi.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Makefile b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Makefile
index 17367bc..72bb42e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Makefile
@@ -16,3 +16,8 @@ ifdef CONFIG_NET_DSA_REALTEK_RTL8366RB_LEDS
 rtl8366-objs 				+= rtl8366rb-leds.o
 endif
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_DSA_REALTEK_RTL8365MB) += rtl8365mb.o
+rtl8365mb-objs := rtl8365mb_main.o \
+		  rtl8365mb_table.o \
+		  rtl8365mb_vlan.o \
+		  rtl8365mb_l2.o \
+# end of rtl8365mb-objs
